From bfff304f4191a5894c0533c6aa0462d321c8eee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fujii Hironori <fujii@igalia.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:21:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [Skia] Pack the SW clip masks of a DDL recording into one
 texture

Tiles are painted by recording a GrDeferredDisplayList on the painting
workers. A recording context cannot use the atlas path renderer, and
GPU tiles have no MSAA, so every anti-aliased clip that is not
analytic (for example an SVG clip-path) is rendered as a CPU mask, and
each mask becomes its own texture, uploaded when the compositor plays
the DDL back. MotionMark Suits draws about a thousand of them per
frame.

When recording a DDL, render masks up to 256x256 into a 1024x1024 CPU
atlas owned by the clip stack and sample them from a single lazy
proxy that uploads the area used by masks on instantiation. The mask
pixels and the sampling (subset, nearest filtering) are unchanged.
Larger masks and direct contexts keep the existing path.

* Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/ClipStack.cpp:
* Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/ClipStack.h:
